// The interpolator, the winding test, and the one-slot exchange.
//
// d3_mix is fx_lerp with a 65536 denominator instead of 1000. The finer parameter
// is not decoration: an edge 400 pixels tall stepped in per-mille advances 2.5
// per-mille per scanline, and the inverse-depth key spans tens of millions, so
// per-mille rounding would put a quarter of a percent of depth error into every
// scanline -- enough to make two nearly-parallel surfaces stripe. 16 bits of
// parameter puts the error below one key unit.

d3_mix(int a, int b, int t) {
  word wp = b;
  wp = (wp - a) * t / 65536;
} return int a + wp;

// Twice the signed area of the screen triangle, as a sign: -1 front-facing, +1
// back-facing, 0 degenerate. The two edge vectors reach 2 * 10^6 pixels after
// d3_pclamp, and their product 4 * 10^12, so this is a word computation -- an int
// one would wrap and report a random winding for exactly the huge off-screen
// triangles a wall makes when the camera is close to it.
d3_area(int[] verts) {
  word wp = verts[6] - verts[0];
  word sm = verts[7] - verts[1];
  wp = wp * (verts[13] - verts[1]) - sm * (verts[12] - verts[0]);
} return int (wp > 0) - (wp < 0);

